<Legal
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The rules of using LeadWave: what you may automate, what we will not let you do, and how billing and cancellation work."
  updated="18 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    By creating a LeadWave account you agree to these terms. They are short on
    purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>What LeadWave is</h2>
  <p>
    A service that connects to a Facebook Page you control and sends messages on
    its behalf according to rules you configure. You remain responsible for what
    those rules say and for what is sent under your Page's name.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be old enough to enter a contract where you live.</li>
    <li>
      You must actually control the Pages you connect. Connecting a Page you do
      not have the right to operate is grounds for immediate termination.
    </li>
    <li>You are responsible for anything done under your account, including by people you invite.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You may not use LeadWave to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Send unsolicited bulk messages, or message people who asked you to stop.</li>
    <li>
      Impersonate another person or business, or operate a Page under a false
      identity.
    </li>
    <li>Distribute malware, run a phishing operation, or solicit credentials or payment details under false pretences.</li>
    <li>
      Circumvent Facebook's rate limits, messaging window or platform policies —
      including by running multiple accounts to get around a limit.
    </li>
    <li>Sell or promote anything illegal where you or your customers are.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We enforce Facebook's messaging window, its one-reply-per-comment rule and a
    shared per-Page send budget in the product itself. These are not optional and
    cannot be turned off.
  </p>

  <h2>Billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Paid plans are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, through our payment
      provider. We never see your card details.
    </li>
    <li>
      Plan limits are enforced, not billed. When you reach a limit we tell you
      and stop; we do not charge overage.
    </li>
    <li>
      Nothing rolls over. AI credits and message allowances reset at the start of
      each cycle.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can cancel at any time and keep access until the end of the period you
      paid for. We do not refund partial periods, except where the law requires
      it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep LeadWave running, but we do not promise it will never be
    unavailable. LeadWave depends on Facebook's Graph API; when that has an
    outage or changes its rules, features can be affected in ways we cannot
    control.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your content is yours. You can export it whenever you like and delete it
    whenever you like. We use it to run the service you asked for, and for
    nothing else. See <a href="/privacy">privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your workspace at any time. We may suspend or terminate an
    account that breaches the acceptable use section above, or that puts our
    Meta platform access at risk — where it is safe and practical to do so, we
    will tell you first and give you a chance to fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    LeadWave is provided as-is. To the extent the law allows, our total liability
    for any claim is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the
    claim. Nothing here limits liability that cannot legally be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms materially we will tell you by email before the
    change takes effect. Continuing to use LeadWave after that means you accept
    the new version.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms — email
    <a href="mailto:leadwaveonline@gmail.com">leadwaveonline@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
